# Architecture guard

Ask, explain, and wait before changing layers, infra, domain, persistence, or packages.

## Frozen map

| Area | Path | Responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Presentation | `apps/web` | React/Next.js UI, hooks, feature folders, API client |
| HTTP / use-case entry | `apps/api/src/modules` | Fastify feature routes |
| Infra adapters | `apps/api/src/plugins`, `apps/api/src/lib` | Cookies, Prisma plugin, Redis |
| Persistence | `packages/database` | Prisma client and schema |
| Infra | `infra/docker` | PostgreSQL, Redis |

## Do not do without approval

- New `packages/*`, `apps/*`, `services/*`, or Docker services
- New layers (`domain/`, `application/`, `infrastructure/`, hexagonal ports)
- Prisma schema / domain model changes
- Moving code across the table above
- Introducing a new ORM, queue, auth provider, or state library

## Do instead

- Extend the existing module/plugin/feature pattern.
- Keep UI out of the API and Prisma out of `apps/web`.
- If a change needs a new boundary, stop and propose it in chat first.
